2026-10-09 19:39:06.547 DEBUG icod.agent.runtime.loop: STEP 4: model responded ->\n  - text: Based on Smartsheet's official API and product architecture, here's the actual schema design:\n\n## Smartsheet Core Data Model\n\n### **Hierarchy Structure**\n```\nAccount/Organization\n  └── Home (root container)\n       ├── Folders (nested, unlimited depth)\n       │    └── Sheets, Reports, Dashboards, Sights\n       └── Sheets, Reports, Dashboards, Sights\n```\n\n### **Sheet Structure** (the core entity)\n```\nSheet\n  ├── id (Long - unique identifier, not auto-increment)\n  ├── name\n  ├── columns[] (ordered array)\n  │    └── Column\n  │         ├── id (Long)\n  │         ├── title (not "name")\n  │         ├── index (position, 0-based)\n  │         ├── type (enum: TEXT_NUMBER, DATE, DATETIME, CHECKBOX, \n  │         │         PICKLIST, CONTACT_LIST, DURATION, PREDECESSOR, ABSTRACT_DATETIME)\n  │         ├── primary (boolean - first column only, always TEXT_NUMBER)\n  │         ├── width (in pixels)\n  │         ├── hidden (boolean)\n  │         ├── locked (boolean)\n  │         ├── options[] (for PICKLIST/CONTACT_LIST types)\n  │         ├── validation (boolean)\n  │         ├── format (formatting rules)\n  │         ├── summary (for summary fields)\n  │         └── systemColumnType (AUTO_NUMBER, MODIFIED_DATE, MODIFIED_BY, CREATED_DATE, CREATED_BY)\n  │\n  ├── rows[] (ordered array)\n  │    └── Row\n  │         ├── id (Long)\n  │         ├── rowNumber (1-based position)\n  │         ├── parentId (for hierarchical/indented rows)\n  │         ├── siblingId (for ordering)\n  │         ├── expanded (boolean, for parent rows)\n  │         ├── cells[] (array of Cell objects)\n  │         │    └── Cell\n  │         │         ├── columnId (Long - references Column.id)\n  │         │         ├── value (string/number/boolean/date - polymorphic)\n  │         │         ├── displayValue (formatted string for UI)\n  │         │         ├── formula (string, if calculated)\n  │         │         ├── hyperlink (object with url/sheetId/reportId)\n  │         │         ├── image (object with image metadata)\n  │         │         ├── contactRef (for CONTACT_LIST columns)\n  │         │         ├── objectValue (complex types like duration, predecessors)\n  │         │         ├── strict (boolean - enforce validation)\n  │         │         └── format (cell-level formatting override)\n  │         ├── attachments[] (file attachments on row)\n  │         ├── discussions[] (row-level discussions/comments)\n  │         ├── conditionalFormat (applied rules)\n  │         ├── createdAt (timestamp)\n  │         ├── modifiedAt (timestamp)\n  │         ├── createdBy (User object)\n  │         └── modifiedBy (User object)\n  │\n  ├── attachments[] (sheet-level attachments)\n  ├── discussions[] (sheet-level discussions)\n  ├── summary (Summary tab - key-value metadata)\n  ├── proofs (approval requests)\n  ├── accesses (sharing permissions)\n  ├── createdAt\n  ├── modifiedAt\n  └── version (integer, increments on changes)\n```\n\n## **Key Differences from Your Current Schema**\n\n### 1. **Cell vs Row.values**\n- **Smartsheet**: Explicit `Cell` table with `columnId` + `value` (normalized)\n- **Yours**: `Row.values` as JSON blob (denormalized)\n- **Impact**: Smartsheet can query/index/filter by specific columns efficiently\n\n### 2. **Column Types**\n- **Smartsheet**: 10+ types including PICKLIST (dropdown), CONTACT_LIST, DURATION, PREDECESSOR\n- **Yours**: 4 types (TEXT, NUMBER, BOOLEAN, DATE)\n- **Missing**: Dropdowns, multi-select, contacts, duration/Gantt dependencies\n\n### 3. **Row Hierarchy**\n- **Smartsheet**: `parentId` enables indented/nested rows (like project tasks with subtasks)\n- **Yours**: Flat row structure\n- **Use case**: WBS, task breakdowns, grouped data\n\n### 4. **Primary Column**\n- **Smartsheet**: First column marked `primary: true`, always visible, used for row identification\n- **Yours**: No primary column concept\n\n### 5. **System Columns**\n- **Smartsheet**: Auto-populated columns (Created Date, Modified By, Auto-Number)\n- **Yours**: `createdAt`/`updatedAt` on row, but not as column types\n\n### 6. **Attachments & Discu... (+1435 chars)
